# AI Assistant Behavior

When helping with this repository:

1. Prefer simple, runnable code over over-engineered research code.
2. Do NOT invent dataset paths, event ids, or channel names. If something is
   unknown, write an inspection script first and verify against the real data.
3. Always preserve the tensor convention `[trials, channels, time]` for saved data.
4. Before implementing a model, check existing configs and the real data shapes.
5. Before modifying training logic, re-read the experiment protocol.
6. For EEG preprocessing, avoid silent assumptions: add logs and sanity checks.
7. For online learning, enforce test-then-update.
8. Never mix source and target subjects in cross-subject experiments.
9. Expose key parameters through YAML configs; keep scripts runnable from the
   project root.
10. Save metrics as CSV/JSON; use clear, descriptive filenames and `run_id`s.
11. Comment the code. Every script/module needs a docstring, and EEG-specific or
    non-obvious choices need an explanatory comment (this project requires comments).
    Comments and docstrings may be in Chinese or English.
12. If a requirement is ambiguous, write a small diagnostic script rather than guess.
13. Respect the server rules: never start heavy/GPU work on the login node; submit
    via Slurm. Never write outside `/share/home/yuan/SYX`; the dataset is read-only.
14. Keep `docs/PROGRESS.md` updated: when you finish a meaningful step or make a
    design decision, append a dated entry. This file is the project's memory.
15. Work in the staged rhythm in `docs/PROJECT_BRIEF.md` (inspect -> preprocess one
    -> validate shape -> preprocess all -> baseline -> 41/10 -> prototype/confidence
    -> fine-tune -> online). Do not jump ahead and build a giant model first.
